  "description": "Explore emergence in .NET: cellular automata (MergeLife, Life-like, Elementary, Cyclic, Wireworld), three flavors of Lenia, fractals (Newton's basins, and Mandelbrot, Julia, and Burning Ship with deep zoom, to 1e9000 for Mandelbrot and Julia), Reynolds boids, and Gray-Scott reaction-diffusion under one consistent API, plus a genetic evolver that searches for new MergeLife rules. Pure C#, netstandard2.1, zero dependencies: it runs anywhere .NET does, including Unity and IL2CPP, and its step and frame APIs allocate nothing. Every system follows a written specification and conformance vectors shared with the Python package, so the same parameters and seed give the same run in either language.",
